    "body": "@Yay295 good point, but tabindex is for the context of the whole page and is only meant for interactive elements. `ord`, assuming that would be the name, can be used on non-interactive elements (like M-'s Box), but more importantly the precedence is not at the page level. Using GitHub again...on this page there are two sets of buttons and both sets have a primary and secondary action (\"Edit\" and \"New issue\" up top, and \"Close with comment\" and \"Comment\" here in the comment box). HTML offers no way of marking the precedence of these buttons.",
