    "body": "> It's a strong signal for spec authors to consider that maybe HTML should step in and offer a standard.\r\n\r\nAgain, the ubiquity of a class is not a reason for HTML to move that _out_ of the perfectly-working `class=\"\"` attribute. If anything, it's a strong signal to _keep_ it there, since it would be disruptive and duplicative to move it out.\r\n\r\nA signal that something needs standardization is instead a set of use cases. Again, see https://whatwg.org/faq#adding-new-features, especially step 1 and 2.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
